Backport RTL8188F chip support (rtl8xxxu_8188f.c + shared/other chip-file
hunks: rtl8xxxu_core.c, rtl8xxxu.h, rtl8xxxu_regs.h, rtl8xxxu_8192c.c,
rtl8xxxu_8192e.c, rtl8xxxu_8723a.c, rtl8xxxu_8723b.c, Kconfig, Makefile)
from upstream mainline v6.2 into our 6.1.84 base -- the onboard
companion/config wifi on the Caddx VRX Pro is a Realtek RTL8188FTV (USB
0bda:f179), confirmed on real hardware. Our 6.1.84 tree's rtl8xxxu only
has a bare RTL8188F enum placeholder, no actual chip-init code or USB ID
registration for it; mainline gained real support shortly after, still
using the same rtl8xxxu_<chip>.c file-naming convention as our tree
(later renamed without the prefix), so v6.2 is the cleanest source to
backport from. The other chip files needed updating too, not just for
8188F support directly, but because v6.2's shared rtl8xxxu.h reworks a
few struct fields/prototypes (e.g. has_xtalk/xtalk -> default_crystal_cap
+ set_crystal_cap() hook) that every chip file references -- taking the
header alone left the untouched chip files referencing removed fields.

Generated by diffing the exact source at our pinned commit (radxa/kernel,
8b0634cfd2bc551f6c0641f30df9cb03f0bd62f0) against torvalds/linux v6.2 for
just this driver directory, then verified with `patch -p1 --dry-run`
against a fresh extraction of our own pinned tarball -- applies cleanly,
no fuzz. One hunk was manually dropped: v6.2's `.wake_tx_queue =
ieee80211_handle_wake_tx_queue` in the ieee80211_ops table doesn't
compile against our 6.1.84 mac80211 core (that helper doesn't exist yet
in this tree) and is unrelated to 8188F support -- an optional callback,
safe to just leave unset as our tree already did pre-patch.

diff -ruN kernel-src-orig/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8xxxu/Kconfig kernel-src-patched/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8xxxu/Kconfig
--- kernel-src-orig/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8xxxu/Kconfig	2026-09-02 16:43:53.539319356 +0200
+++ kernel-src-patched/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8xxxu/Kconfig	2026-09-02 16:47:40.996973088 +0200
@@ -3,13 +3,14 @@
 # RTL8XXXU Wireless LAN device configuration
 #
 config RTL8XXXU
-	tristate "RTL8723AU/RTL8188[CR]U/RTL819[12]CU (mac80211) support"
+	tristate "Realtek 802.11n USB wireless chips support"
 	depends on MAC80211 && USB
 	help
 	  This is an alternative driver for various Realtek RTL8XXX
 	  parts written to utilize the Linux mac80211 stack.
 	  The driver is known to work with a number of RTL8723AU,
-	  RL8188CU, RTL8188RU, RTL8191CU, and RTL8192CU devices
+	  RL8188CU, RTL8188RU, RTL8191CU, RTL8192CU, RTL8723BU, RTL8192EU,
+	  and RTL8188FU devices.
 
 	  This driver is under development and has a limited feature
 	  set. In particular it does not yet support 40MHz channels
@@ -22,7 +23,7 @@
 	  but you will need to control which module you wish to load.
 
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module will
-	  be called r8xxxu.  If unsure, say N.
+	  be called rtl8xxxu.  If unsure, say N.
 
 config RTL8XXXU_UNTESTED
 	bool "Include support for untested Realtek 8xxx USB devices (EXPERIMENTAL)"
